WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.980
The Second Plate
Episode 8

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.400
Soma-kun, are you going somewhere?

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.030
Oh, sorry!

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.860
Did I wake you?

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:15.820
What're you doing so early before dawn?

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:18.030
Quick trip the fish market.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.390
The fish market!

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.040
You're going to check out Pacific saury!

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.960
The fish market!

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.060
Hey, can I tag along?

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.720
Sure! Come!

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.980
I'll go get ready!

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.170
I'll be waiting outside.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.180
First, I have to figure out what to make.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.390
I'm gonna find the key to
defeating Kurokiba and Hayama!

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:10.870
Battle of Seasonality

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.010
Outta the way!
Battle of Seasonality

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.100
How much for a kilo?!
Battle of Seasonality

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.500
Gimme the big one in the back!
Battle of Seasonality

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:14.780
Gimme the big one in the back!

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.180
Wow!

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:17.860
It's so lively!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.820
This is really exciting!

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.450
Oh, the yellowtail amberjack's cheap.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.860
The horse mackerel, too.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.240
Soma-kun!

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.670
Don't you think the other fish
can wait until next time?

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.000
Oh, right.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.380
Soma-kun, have you ever been here before?

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.570
Yeah, I came with my dad a lot.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.340
Oh, there it is! Pacific saury!

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.560
I gotta say, this time I think the recipe
testing process will be pretty smooth.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.150
Yukihira Diner

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.810
Pacific saury was always
on our fall menu at Yukihira.
Yukihira Diner

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.890
Miso Mackerel Set Menu
Grilled Fish Set Menu (Salmon, Mackerel, Atka Mackerel)
Pacific Saury Set Meal    Daily Special Set Menu
Pacific saury was always
on our fall menu at Yukihira.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.750
So I'm pretty confident
when it comes to Pacific saury.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.030
Oh.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.500
Kurokiba-kun, Nakiri-san?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.780
You came to look at Pacific saury, too?

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.510
What a coincidence!

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.270
What coincidence?

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.000
I've been coming here practically every day.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.370
Huh.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.830
Me, I only come sometimes.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.810
The fish market's open
too early in the morning!

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:15.840
Oh, no!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.510
Why'd we have to come
face to face with his opponent?!

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.870
I can't take a back seat to you guys!

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:24.130
I'd better find myself some good
Pacific saury, and get ahead!

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.820
Pacific saury should have a
rounded body with taut flesh,

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.970
eyes that are clear and bright,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.730
and mouths with a yellow tip.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.610
It's said that means it's fresh
and has good fat.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:41.250
But it doesn't mean you should
just spring for the freshest ones.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.450
Then their umami hasn't fully developed.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.160
Inosinic acid, the umami component
in fish, increases over time.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.830
The amount and development rate
of inosinic acid

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.380
are dependent on the conditions
when the fish was caught.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.880
You need a certain amount of experience

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.840
to gauge the fish's freshness and umami.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.720
Oh, but it's not just about
gauging with the eye.

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.460
There's a way to tell by feel, too!

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:07.180
Look!

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.570
Oh, wow!

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.600
Even though you're holding it by the tail,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.060
it's standing straight up!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.020
It's proof that the flesh is still firm!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.400
The eyes and belly look fresh, too.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.280
Without a doubt, this is the best
Pacific saury this shop has to offer today!

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.160
You're wrong.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.360
I'll take this one.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:30.100
What?

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.080
That?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.780
It's smaller than Soma-kun's Pacific saury,

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.210
and the belly's flatter than his, too.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:40.410
You don't look convinced.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:41.840
Do you want to put them to the test?

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.400
If we make sashimi with these two fish,

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.550
you can tell which one's of higher quality,

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:50.960
and which one of us
has the more discerning eye.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.750
Sorry for doing this at your storefront.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.070
Oh, it's fine, since they're Totsuki students.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.790
Try them, Tadokoro Megumi.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.950
Soma-kun's Pacific saury... is less firm.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:33.640
Kurokiba-kun's Pacific saury
has firmer flesh, but why?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.900
That's why there is a time lag
between that fish's rigor index

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.560
and breaking strength of the fish's flesh.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.830
For Pacific saury, the rigor index, which
is the indicator of how firm the flesh is,

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.860
gradually decreases after an average of ten hours
after the fish was subjected to ikejime.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.390
Time (hours)
Rigor
Index
(%)
gradually decreases after an average of ten hours
after the fish was subjected to ikejime.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.850
But what determines mouthfeel
is the muscle's breaking strength.
Rigor
Index
(%)
Time (hours)

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:55.410
That rapidly plummets after
approximately five hours.
Rigor
Index
(%)
Time (hours)

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.230
That means, even if the flesh feels firm,

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:02.140
it may already have poor mouthfeel
if more than five hours have passed?

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.230
Yes, it's a pitfall when
picking Pacific saury.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.090
Well, not that it matters to me.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.420
What's with that?!

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.890
I went through the trouble
of explaining it for you!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.900
I can tell by looking and touching it.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.330
I can tell how it was swimming in the sea,

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.470
how good the ikejime technique was,

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.480
and whether enough ice was used
when transporting the fish.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.230
I can tell everything.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.420
Listen, Yukihira.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.890
When something's in season,
the quality of the ingredient and its flavor

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:30.530
dramatically increase to incomparable levels.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.010
The flip side of that is,

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:34.240
if you can't get the best,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.200
you're already putting yourself
at a big disadvantage.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.100
The reason I keep going to the fish market

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.800
is that my feel for ingredients will dull

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.630
if I spend even a short time away.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.380
It's been ten years now.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.010
That's how I've lived my life.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.960
I won't take a back seat to someone

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.170
who's judging quality
with half-assed knowledge.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.580
Excuse us.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.060
Now that I think about,

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.440
another Totsuki student was here earlier.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.340
Oh, I saw him, too!

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.380
That tanned-looking hottie, right?

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:15.700
He was walking sort of looking down
when he suddenly stopped in his tracks, and...

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:18.890
Excuse me.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.860
I want the middle one in the front box,

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.870
and the one second
from the left in the back box.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:27.880
He chose my best fish of the day
without even taking a look!

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:29.500
Wow.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.970
I bet hotties have good instincts!

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.930
So I guess they're much better than me
at judging ingredients.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.560
If I can't get the best,

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.230
I'm already at a huge disadvantage, huh...

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:47.920
It's done.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:48.480
Yeah.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.950
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:57.840
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.200
It's so good!
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn
Autumn

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.930
Guess this is the power
of it being in season.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:08.170
But I bet those two will find even better ones
than this on the day of the match.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.370
If you're going to try to reach their level,

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:15.130
you'll have to come here every day to study.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:15.720
Yeah.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:18.930
But it'll be tough.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:21.670
Dad!

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:22.140
Yeah?

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:25.700
Hey, Soma. That sardine is no good.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:26.290
Huh?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.170
Why?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.940
Each type of fish has a million
different pointers for its quality.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.450
Even if you're only talking about one fish,

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.830
it'll take more than ten years
to be good at judging them.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.250
Crap!

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.090
What a laugh.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:43.560
I have less than ten days to go
until the match.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:46.960
Besides, even if I get better
at choosing the fish,

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.800
it won't mean anything if I slack
on brainstorming what dish to make.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.190
You're right.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:58.640
I bet those two will make dishes that'll
maximize the best ingredients they can find.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.660
What should I do?

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.100
Even now, those two are...

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:06.560
I guess I'm in trouble.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:12.680
Professor Shiomi, can you tell us what
kind of assistant Hayama-kun is to you?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:13.850
Uh...

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.490
Um, H-Hayama-kun is v-v-very competent!

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:22.070
He's an excellent a-a-assistant.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.230
Um, so, er, well, uh...
Don't get so nervous over
a simple interview, Jun.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.000
You're such a research nerd.
Um, so, er, well, uh...

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.250
Don't call me Jun!

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.750
Hayama-kun, is it true that you can tell
which Pacific saury is good

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.460
just from the smell alone?

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.710
Yes.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:39.760
The smell of fish comes from
aldehydes and other components.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.980
They are produced when
polyunsaturated fatty acid oxidizes.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.440
My nose can detect the volatile compounds
released as a precursor to that process.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.720
It can also detect the stench of blood,

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.650
and how much umami has developed.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.730
Ingredients give off a lot of information.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.160
Not only can I smell how fresh they are,

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:04.080
I can figure out which Pacific saury
will be best for my specific dish.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.510
Hey, Mitsuru.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.580
Did you finish interviewing Yukihira?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.120
N-No.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.350
He hasn't come back from the fish market yet.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.000
I don't think he's started
testing recipes yet.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.390
So he's behind.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:22.850
I figured Yukihira wasn't up to the task.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.140
Just like most predicted,

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.970
looks like it'll be a face-off
between Hayama and Kurokiba.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:28.800
Kitchen No. 5

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.690
Kurokiba-kun, Hayama-kun seems to be
preparing himself at a steady pace,
Kitchen No. 5

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.830
Kurokiba-kun, Hayama-kun seems to be
preparing himself at a steady pace,

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.070
but Yukihira-kun seems to be struggling.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.610
Do you feel it's safe to say that you
have one less rival to worry about?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.610
I don't consider them rivals.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.830
I don't care about Yukihira or Hayama.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:43.910
I'm the one who'll win, anyway.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:48.370
I'm sorry, can you speak up a little louder?

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.040
You're going to use all this
in the Pacific saury dish?

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.800
How long are you going to stick around?!

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.510
Get out!

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.260
H-He said we could interview him earlier!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.220
Do
Not
Enter

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.220
They'd better not be thinking

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.520
that they've reached my level
just because of that curry match!

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.150
Yukihira...

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:12.920
...and...

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.070
There's no heat from you about our battle.

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.270
Kurokiba Ryo...

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.070
I'll burn you both into cinders.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:26.330
I'm gonna redeem myself from the
humiliating defeat at the semi-finals.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.270
It's hard to imagine
how I could lose against you.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.750
Hayama!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.830
I'm the one who'll win!

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.300
Sorry, Fumio-san!

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:39.990
Thank you for coming to pick us up.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.390
No worries.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.180
Doing well in the Autumn Elections

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:46.380
improves Polar Star Dormitory's prestige.

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:52.660
But it looks like he's
hitting a wall of some sort.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:53.270
Yes.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.110
Soma-kun's been like this for a while.

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:00.240
It's true that the cards
are pretty stacked against you

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.310
when you're up against
two such discerning opponents.

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.040
If the playing field was a little more even,

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:07.150
there are ways to narrow
the gap in small ways.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:07.910
Ways?

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.880
For example, when you'll salt the fish.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:11.910
The taste will change

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.880
depending on how long you salt the
Pacific saury before cooking it.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.460
I see.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.420
The salt will draw out the water
and make the flesh firmer.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.840
It's the same principle as light pickling.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:25.180
You can also expect the umami to increase.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.720
On the flip side, if you let it rest
for too long after salting,

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.140
you'll lose out on the freshness.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:32.800
Time, huh...

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:37.250
When it's freshly caught,
there's not enough umami.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.610
But the more time passes,
the less fresh it'll become.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.650
It's often said that fish
tastes the best when it's overripe...

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:48.830
Wait a minute...

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.390
Ibusaki, there you are!

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.210
Sakaki!

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.340
Are you here?!

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:02.790
Huh?

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:10.140
Nikumi!

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.700
Huh?! Yukihira?

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:15.060
Please come with me, Nikumi.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.590
Huh? With you?

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.190
Sorry for asking you all to come here.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.070
What's going on, Yukihira-kun?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.070
Not this again.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.590
You have no chance of winning
unless you can get the best Pacific saury

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:30.910
on the day of the match, right?

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:33.660
I'm not going to go to the
fish market in the morning.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.870
What?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.620
What do you mean, Soma-kun?

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:40.460
I'll go buy my Pacific saury
a couple of days before the match.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.700
I won't have much time to experiment,

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.970
but if I succeed, at the match itself,

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.470
I can have Pacific saury that surpasses
what the season has to offer!

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:49.750
So you mean...

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:50.430
And so...

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.470
I'm going to age the fish!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.330
Age the fish...

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:55.870
I see!

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.610
Ryoko-chan specializes in rice malt,

00:13:57.610 --> 00:13:59.460
and Ibusaki-kun in smoking.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:02.020
They're all experts in aging methods!

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.460
Nikumi is an expert, too.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.890
You're up to speed
on trendy aged meats, aren't you?

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:08.580
Yeah. You're talking about aged beef?

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.630
It involves controlling
the temperature and humidity

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:13.450
while air-drying and resting meat.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:17.490
The flavor of ingredients isn't
necessarily dependent on freshness.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:21.470
If I can succeed in aging the fish
to bring out its umami,

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:24.230
I bet I can compete with
their ability to judge fish!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.050
So, can you guys please help me?

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:28.180
Yeah!

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.000
Of course!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.260
We eat at the same table! We're family!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.890
Yeah! It's worth a shot!

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.060
You'll help too, right, Ibusaki-kun?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.020
Well, sure, I guess.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:40.270
All right!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.900
Let's start testing!

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.020
Yeah!

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.900
Ah, youth...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:47.690
9 Days Until the Match

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.860
I'll try three aging methods:
9 Days Until the Match

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.220
salted rice malt,

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.230
smoking,

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:55.910
and a high-humidity refrigerator.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.700
Thanks for lending this to me, Nikumi.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.870
I-It's nothing!

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:05.850
About the aging period, it's best
to let it rest at least three days.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.620
I'd say about the same
length of time for smoking.

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.810
Drying and salting take two days,

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:11.890
and curing will take one whole day.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:15.390
The fridge will also finish the job
in about three, four days.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:16.850
I see.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.260
With those timelines,

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:21.620
you can test each method twice.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.330
Yeah, but only twice.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.020
Will that be enough to surpass
their ability to judge fish?

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:27.400
It'll be intense.

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:32.860
You have to make sure that the
rice malt penetrates the fish.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.200
It's important to control
the temperature, too.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:37.450
The type of saumur liquid
and fumigant you use

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.330
will both slightly affect the curing process.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:44.560
By letting it rest at 3C and 90% humidity,

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.440
you'll lose just the
right amount of moisture,

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.800
which will concentrate the umami.

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:53.050
Great!

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:57.050
All three of them will be done
in three days.

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:59.500
I'm going to take advantage of this wait time

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:02.100
and do everything I can.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.450
It's finally done.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:18.830
6 Days Until the Match
It's finally done.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.750
Yeah! The aged Pacific saury
tests are all done!
6 Days Until the Match

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.210
Well, no point in waiting!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.050
They're great!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.180
All of them have a vastly improved umami.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:36.590
They're all great!

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:36.700
The salted rice malt one has
a mellow and gentle depth of flavor.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.300
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
The salted rice malt one has
a mellow and gentle depth of flavor.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:40.330
In terms of fragrance,
the smoked one is the best!
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.070
Smoked Pacific Saury
In terms of fragrance,
the smoked one is the best!
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:42.200
The one aged in high-humidity conditions
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
Smoked Pacific Saury

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.550
Pacific Saury Aged in
High-Humidity Conditions
The one aged in high-humidity conditions
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
Smoked Pacific Saury

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:46.200
can be used in a lot of
different dishes, too.
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
Smoked Pacific Saury
Pacific Saury Aged in
High-Humidity Conditions

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:50.230
Baked in foil, fried and marinated,
or broiled. They all sound good.
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
Smoked Pacific Saury
Pacific Saury Aged in
High-Humidity Conditions

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.030
I bet it'd be great if you just
make sushi with this, too!
Pacific Saury
Pickled with Salted Rice Malt
Smoked Pacific Saury
Pacific Saury Aged in
High-Humidity Conditions

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:53.650
But...

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:59.070
I still think Kurokiba-kun's
Pacific saury back at the fish market

00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.370
tasted better.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.530
Yeah, I thought so.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:04.650
But it's been aged perfectly!

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:06.780
This still isn't enough?

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.230
Hey, Tadokoro.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:14.260
Tell Yukihira something for me.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:18.140
He can call me if he ever needs help.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:19.340
Okay!

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.630
Later.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:22.590
Good night, Mito-san.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:32.900
Was it pointless to try using aging
methods to surpass their Pacific saury?

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:37.560
Should I use the rest of my time
to study how to judge fish?

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:41.030
No... it's too soon to give up on aging.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:45.220
All the Pacific saury I tested
had much stronger umami.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.370
I'm on the right track here.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:50.740
I only have one more round of testing left.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:53.700
After that, I have to prepare
for the actual match.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.590
What should I test?

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:59.780
Something better than rice malt, curing,
or high-humidity aging...

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.020
What would let me surpass those two?

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.670
Think.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.930
What's better?

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:13.160
I need a catalyst for aging Pacific saury.
Something to develop its umami!

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:20.280
Time to go buy Pacific saury.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.210
What's wrong, Yukihira?

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:25.790
Why the long face?

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:29.650
You're not gonna get any decent
testing done like that.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.460
Stand up straight, won't you?

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.590
What, are you lecturing me while
enjoying your nighttime sake?

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:36.990
Well, in times like that,

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.620
it's important to stop what you're doing.

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:46.810
I love you, Fumio-san!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.470
Hey!

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.770
You're going to spill my sake!

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.160
Looks like you have an idea, Yukihira.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.010
Yeah!

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.180
It just might work!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:59.780
Day of the Match: Early Morning

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.620
Yukihira Soma isn't here today, either.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.570
What's his game?

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:07.580
He hasn't been here in days.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.920
Did he give up on the match?

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:10.670
...No.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.380
He's better than that.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.120
What's he planning?

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:24.050
Autumn Elections
Main Tournament Finals

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:26.090
Thank you for waiting, everyone!
Autumn Elections
Main Tournament Finals

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:28.230
It's the Autumn Elections Finals!
Autumn Elections
Main Tournament Finals

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:31.060
The three candidates will enter the arena!
Autumn Elections
Main Tournament Finals

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.820
The Prince of Aroma, Candidate Hayama Akira!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.030
The Dictator of the Kitchen,
Candidate Kurokiba Ryo!

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:49.580
And the third, from the downtown diner,
Candidate Yukihira Soma!

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.180
Yukihira!

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:55.210
We've got your back!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:56.850
You can do it!

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.430
I believe in you!

00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:02.720
We'll now begin the Autumn Election Finals!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.970
Allow me to introduce to you
our honored judges today.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.240
Oh, Isshiki-senpai.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:11.730
It's hard to recognize him
when he's wearing clothes.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:15.500
Forget that. Did Yukihira finish
developing his dish?

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.150
Well, none of us actually knows.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.440
I see.

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:25.530
First, serving as the chair is
Academy Director Nakiri Senzaemon-dono.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.590
Executive Chef of Totsuki Resort
and head of the tourism division,

00:20:30.590 --> 00:20:32.120
Dojima Gin-senpai.

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.080
And we have one more:

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.710
head of Nakiri International,
Totsuki's research division,

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.270
Nakiri Leonora-dono!

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:43.560
She's beautiful!

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:44.840
She's so fair!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.470
I wonder if she's Scandinavian.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:47.680
Oh, my mom.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:48.570
What?!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:53.000
Leonora-dono leads Nakiri International,

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.460
an academic institute that
conducts research on gourmet food

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.860
and molecular gastronomy,
using cutting edge technology.

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:02.550
Would you be so kind as to say a few words?

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:11.290
G-Good day, everyone!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:14.110
I am Nakiri Leonora, yes.

00:21:14.110 --> 00:21:16.120
I live in Denmark!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.400
Judging feels hard,

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:19.960
but I'll try my best!

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.510
Her Japanese is horrible!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.920
Mother, you should at least tell me
when you're coming to Japan!

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.070
Hey, Alice.

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:27.970
Only staff can be in here!

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:30.760
Oh, Alice, good to see you.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.810
Erina-chan, you too.

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:36.140
You're super angry, as usual.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.690
It's because of your daughter!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:42.230
You're Yukihira-kun,
who defeated my daughter?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.940
I was big surprised!

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:48.740
That's why I'm looking forward
to your dish, okay?

00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:54.170
If it's not good, I might get mad-angry!

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:28.420
First, let us see each
candidate's Pacific saury

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:35.810
What exquisite shine and firmness.

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:37.940
They have nice fat, too.

00:23:37.940 --> 00:23:39.770
They are like drawn blades!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:43.980
Like famed swords, suitable for the finals!

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:44.970
Shit!

00:23:44.970 --> 00:23:46.980
How can he win against fish like <i>that</i>?!

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:48.070
Soma-kun...

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:55.410
What?!

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:56.310
What is that?
What?!

00:23:56.310 --> 00:23:56.900
What is that?

00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:58.190
It doesn't look...

00:23:58.190 --> 00:23:59.880
...like it's any kind of sword!

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:05.520
Next Episode: A Sword that Signals Autumn
